      "sha": "649b2e5eba37f03e14e7dbbbc2079fbad2e3e03e",
      "message": "fix: isolate cache writes of pull request triggered reusable workflows (#1793)\n\nA reusable workflow (`workflow_call`) triggered by a pull request can write cache\nentries that later trusted runs restore. `getWriteIsolationKey` assigns the pull\nrequest write isolation key only for the `pull_request` event name, but the server\nrewrites the event name of reusable jobs to `workflow_call` for input evaluation\nwhile retaining the original ref (`refs/pull/N/head`) and pull request payload in\nthe task context. A reusable job triggered by a pull request therefore falls\nthrough to the empty (trusted) isolation key and can plant cache entries that\ntrusted runs (pushes to the default branch, manual dispatch) later restore.\n\nCo-authored-by: Robin Everaars <redacted@example.invalid>\nReviewed-on: https://code.forgejo.org/forgejo/runner/pulls/1793\nReviewed-by: Mathieu Fenniak <redacted@example.invalid>\n",
      "author": {
